URL Parsing and Host Validation Issues Improper handling of URL parsing or host validation can lead to attackers providing malformed URLs that bypass intended domain checks, potentially redirecting users to malicious sites., Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR) via Host Manipulation If the host validation logic is not robust, an attacker might be able to craft a target URL that appears to be within the domain (e.g., using a different TLD or a cleverly crafted subdomain) but is actually controlled by them, leading to redirection to an attacker-controlled resource.

